{"kind":"assert","text":"Accepted: the failed-claim creation cohort (8a8902f3) is the default for new rooms on dap-demo\n\nAll four done conditions hold:\n1. Scripted host failures: the cohort source landed under 12a718fe. Its failed-claim owner gives each failed claim a final failed state, frees its place and lets new rooms start.\n2. A scratch room on a deployed Worker: on 7 November a scratch room on dap-demo's Register 26 ran through the real commands. Its one-hour read token cloned the room, and after the hour the provider refused the same token with HTTP 403. The live record landed at 903ed961.\n3. The default: dap install's default plan and the Page offer both name platform:register@26 on dap-demo. dap-demo has deployed from the checked-in configuration since 9d96cf25.\n4. Existing rooms keep their pins: in the J5 room, child birth, clone and Site all passed after the switch, with every pin unchanged.\n\nThe limits that 991129fc names close in the cohort source (checker-key invitations, journal export, the Page offer and apps/views, and replay from the new pins' bytes). The three limits in 4d9a50e8 stay accepted. The live record names the creation pins on each Worker.\n\nTwo limits stay, with reasons:\n- The live replay from the deployed scratch room did not run, because that room has no journal archive binding. Local export, mirror clone and offline verification from the new pins' bytes cover replay.\n- dap-grow and dap-lending keep their registers. dap-grow's archive bridge checks one root, so switching it needs that bridge fixed first.\n\ndocs/deploy.md states that existing dap-demo rooms stay on Register 17 and new rooms use Register 26. The planner closes 8a8902f3 by superseding it with this acceptance.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}